  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jackson Merrill swung twice and the game was over.",
    "what_this_means": "This team doesn't need drama when it has production in front of it. Merrill's two home runs transformed a tied game into a blowout by the fifth inning, and once the margin opened, there was no tension left to manufacture. The offense made 16 hits count. Converting five of eleven RISP situations into runs across four innings of heavy scoring. Kyle Hart pitched 2.1 scoreless innings to bridge the early exit. That's not a pattern that breaks often. The win streak is four now because when the lineup connects like this, the pitching holds, and nothing gets left on the table. They extended a streak that looked fragile a week ago into something real.",
